      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Baseline TiVNbTa has approximately 800 MPa room-temperature yield strength and approximately 40% strain.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Baseline TiVNbTa has approximately 330 MPa yield strength and 423 MPa compressive strength at 1273 K and 30% strain.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Post-sintering annealing at approximately 600–800 °C for several hours can nucleate and control coherent nanometer-scale precipitates in TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An inert or vacuum annealing environment will avoid oxidation.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled cooling will retain a fine precipitate size.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed treatment will produce a stable, uniformly distributed dispersion of coherent precipitates in the TiVNbTa BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fine second-phase particles can strengthen BCC HEAs.",
